<title>MEXICO: RESEARCH ALERT-Cifra cut on Wal-Mart offer.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Cifra cut on Wal-Mart offer.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch said in a research report it had lowered its intermediate recommendation on Mexican retailer Cifra's A and B series voting shares to neutral from accumulate.</p>
<p>-- The firm lowered the rating after Cifra recommended that shareholders sell their stock to Wal-Mart Stores Inc at their tender offer of $2.03 per share, analysts Robert Ford and Melissa Byun wrote in the July 29 report.</p>
<p>-- Nonetheless, the analysts said they kept their intermediate accumulate recommendation on the non-voting C shares and their long-term buy on all series.</p>
<p>(( -- Martin Roberts, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7907))</p>
